SwiftPutty local patch 0011
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   not yet reported upstream; suitable for upstream

Proxy: free the proxy socket's copy of the Conf when it closes.

new_connection() gives each ProxySocket its own conf_copy(), which the
negotiators read (proxy host and port, SOCKS 5 user name and password),
but sk_proxy_close() never frees it, so every proxied connection leaked
a whole Conf. Found by `leaks --atExit` on Core/tests/spb_backends_test.c,
whose sessions go through SOCKS 4/5, HTTP, Telnet and local proxies.

--- a/proxy/proxy.c
+++ b/proxy/proxy.c
@@ -103,6 +103,7 @@
     sk_addr_free(ps->remote_addr);
     proxy_negotiator_cleanup(ps);
     bufchain_clear(&ps->output_from_negotiator);
+    conf_free(ps->conf);
     sfree(ps);
 }
 
